# Privacy Policy

**Last updated:** 8 October 2026

**Operator:** Ezigboe ("we", "us", "our")
**App:** Zynq ("the App")
**Contact:** info@ezigboe.com

This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, share, and protect information when you use the Zynq mobile application and related services.

By using Zynq, you agree to this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree, please do not use the App.

---

## 1. Who this policy applies to

Zynq is intended **only for users aged 18 and older**. We do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under 18. If you believe a minor has created an account, contact us at info@ezigboe.com and we will delete it.

---

## 2. Information we collect

### 2.1 Information you provide

- **Account:** email address and password, or the name and email address Google shares when you sign in with Google; display name, date of birth, gender, bio, photos, interests, dating preferences, and discovery settings.
- **Profile:** photos you upload; optional voice-prompt recordings; optional profile video; an optional, unverified salary band you choose from a list; optional prompt-game answers, and whether you choose to show those answers on your profile.
- **Verification:** photos or video you submit for identity review, if you use verification.
- **Messages:** messages you send to matches, including text and gifts; messages you post in communities, including text, images, and voice notes.
- **Safety:** Zynq user IDs of trusted contacts you add; details of a date you choose to share (place and time) when both people have opted in; the fact that you started a panic alert or a date-share session.
- **Reputation:** behavior ratings you submit about someone you have interacted with, and ratings others submit about you. We turn those ratings into a profile tag that can be shown on a profile.
- **Events and house parties:** registration details, and content you post in a house-party context.
- **Support:** information you send in a support ticket or a user report.

### 2.2 Information collected automatically

- **Approximate location,** if you allow it: we use it to show a coarse distance label (how far away someone is) and to improve discovery. Other users see that label, not your exact coordinates, for ordinary discovery.
- **Precise location,** only while a safety session you start is active and only if you have allowed location access: latitude and longitude, and the time of that reading. We share those coordinates with the trusted contacts you chose, as described in section 4.
- **Chat activity:** message timing and reply length, used to show priority marks and activity summaries. You can control whether chat activity is visible, where the App offers that setting.
- **Usage:** swipes, likes, passes, matches, gifts sent and received, event and party activity, community membership, and similar in-app actions stored on our servers.
- **Device and technical data:** device type, operating system, app version, Firebase Cloud Messaging token for push notifications, and diagnostic and analytics data via Firebase.

### 2.3 Microphone, camera, and photos

- **Microphone:** used only when you record a voice prompt or a voice note. We store the recording you choose to send or save.
- **Camera and photos:** used for profile photos, verification media, images you send, and QR check-in at events we host.

You can deny or revoke these permissions in device settings. Features that need them will not work without them.

### 2.4 Purchases

Gold and Platinum subscriptions, and consumable gift bundles, are sold through **Google Play** and, where offered, the **Apple App Store**. We receive the product identifier, purchase token or receipt, and confirmation of the purchase. We do not receive your payment card number. There is no coin wallet and no virtual currency.

### 2.5 Rephrase

If you use Rephrase, the draft text and the tone you select are sent to **Google Gemini** to generate a suggested rewrite. The suggestion is not saved to your profile or message until you accept it. Do not submit anything in a draft that you are not willing to send to that service.

